The original Behler–Parrinello cutoff function is piecewise: fc(Rij) = 0.5[cos(π Rij / Rc) + 1] for Rij ≤ Rc, and 0 for Rij > Rc [W2025444507#004]. The π is garbled in the extracted text of that passage, but the ANI-1 passage gives the same form as 0.5 × cos(π Rij / RC) + 0.5 for Rij ≤ RC [W2541404351#007]. Beyond Rc the function has zero value and zero slope [W2025444507#004]. The original paper used Rc = 6 Å [W2025444507#005].


